[issue.1751]
number = 1751
title = "[Coherence] evidence_inventory now refuses any tenant whose legacy receipt evidence was archived by the existing migration path, so migrated tenants can no longer recover"
revision = "a910fdedd579e63379ae6c2e4d4971990d28f8ad"
verdict = "duplicate"
evidence = "Issue #1737 already describes the same migrated-receipt archive blocking tenant recovery at spec/layerx-merge/programme/issues/input/1737.md:5: services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/receipt.rs:426 and services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/receipt.rs:741 preserve legacy archives, the inventory refusal introduced by commit 8950f604bf7a698a739df93a15148ac30e702ef5 remains at services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/receipt.rs:528 before current-evidence handling at services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/receipt.rs:549, services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/human_runtime.rs:14438 and services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/human_runtime.rs:14795 propagate that refusal to policy budget reads and recovery, and services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/repair_22_31_364.rs:683 and services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/repair_22_31_364.rs:693 still require inventory after migration and reopening, although services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/tests/repair_22_31_559.rs:589 seeds an archive beside public version 1 evidence rather than the public version 2 evidence migration writes at services/agent/crates/layerx-agentd/src/receipt.rs:779."
close_comment = "Closing as a duplicate of #1737, which covers the same conflict between authenticated receipt migration and the legacy-archive refusal that blocks tenant inventory and budget recovery. Migrated receipts must remain recoverable from authenticated evidence while unsupported records remain refused."
